{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3192","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3192","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3192\",\"parent_revision\":\"a271839f2def514e50d91918126b6b8a5acb98de7662e79f41b04cb6cca4dc39\",\"root_revision\":\"a271839f2def514e50d91918126b6b8a5acb98de7662e79f41b04cb6cca4dc39\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`ArtifactStatus` (plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:1582) only defines `draft`, `current`, `superseded`, `archived`. `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__artifact_register`'s `status` parameter constructs `ArtifactStatus(status)` from the passed value and raises `ValueError` for any value outside that set (plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:~3370).\\n\\nNine agent/skill files instruct or literally call `artifact_register(..., status=\\\"complete\\\", ...)`, which is not a member of `ArtifactStatus` and will raise at runtime:\\n\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md:172\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md:173\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/t0-baseline-capture.md:141\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/codebase-analyzer.md:741 (checklist item, not a live call)\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/reviewer-performance.md:135\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/reviewer-accessibility.md:142\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/tn-verification-gate.md:156\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md:383,426\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/reviewer-quality.md:131\\n\\nConfirmed pre-existing on `origin/main` (not introduced by the plan-file-model-dh refactor) \u2014 same enum definition on main has no `complete` member. Verified independently by reading `models.py` on both `origin/main` and the target branch.\\n\\nLikely intended value is `current` (the default) given these are all \\\"finished capturing this artifact\\\" registrations, not literally a distinct `complete` lifecycle state that exists in the enum.\\n\\nOut of scope for PR #3159 (that PR only touches 3 of these 9 files, and fixing this systemically means editing files far outside that PR's diff) \u2014 flagging as its own item per repo's Pre-Existing Issue Accountability rule rather than silently expanding PR #3159's diff.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered while addressing PR #3159 review findings (fix/verify pass on refactor/plan-file-model-dh)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4bf178cdb68c3ee7206add3c0ddc2e7a53ece5eabdb9f3060916656195a984ca\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQTRz1Q\"}"}